8. How do you switch from one user to another?
Use the su command.

Command:
// su - devopsuser
or
// sudo su - devopsuser

Use Case:
Testing application permissions with another user account.

9. How do you delete a user in Linux?
Use the userdel command.
Command:
// sudo userdel devopsuser

Delete user along with home directory:
sudo userdel -r devopsuser

10. What is the difference between Root User and Normal User?
Root User	                  Normal User
Full system access	  Limited access
Can install software	Cannot install without permission
Can manage all users	Cannot manage other users


# Q. Why is User and Group Management important in Cloud & DevOps?
Answer:
User and Group Management helps implement security and access control. In DevOps environments, different teams (Developers, Testers, DevOps Engineers) require different permissions.

> Example:
Developers → Deploy applications
Testers → Access test environment only
DevOps Team → Manage servers and CI/CD pipelines